1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,820
Is there anything nicer than a cooling ice cream on a hot summer's day?
还有什么比在炎热夏日里来一份清凉的冰淇淋更惬意的事吗？

2
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:15,340
This traditional treat is centuries old, but our tastes and consumer habits are evolving.
这种传统美食已有数百年历史，但我们的口味和消费习惯却在不断演变。

3
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:23,290
How is the ice cream production process changing, and who is driving this change?
冰淇淋的生产流程正发生着怎样的变化？又是谁在推动这些变化呢？

4
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:27,990
Making ice cream is a time-consuming process.
制作冰淇淋是一个耗时的过程。

5
00:00:27,990 --> 00:00:38,570
While the recipe is simple – milk, sugar and fat, plus flavours and colours – ice cream has a complex chemistry.
尽管配方很简单——牛奶、糖、脂肪，再加上调味剂和色素——但冰淇淋的制作却涉及复杂的化学变化。

6
00:00:38,570 --> 00:00:49,070
Getting the balance right between ice, fat and air is important if the ice cream is to have the right texture.
要让冰淇淋拥有恰到好处的口感，关键在于平衡好冰、脂肪和空气三者的比例。

7
00:00:49,070 --> 00:01:02,890
To achieve this, the ingredients need to be mixed and heated, then cooled and frozen – a process that takes time and uses a lot of energy.
为了达到这个效果，原料需要经过混合、加热，再冷却、冷冻，整个过程既耗时又耗能。

8
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:13,340
Designers and engineers are working to improve the production process with new specialised equipment to make it increasingly automated.
设计师和工程师们正研发新型专业设备来改进生产流程，使其自动化程度越来越高。

9
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:28,610
For now, however, even with the help of robots and 3D printers, it can take up to two years from testing a new frozen dessert product to it being available to consumers.
不过目前，即便有机器人和3D打印机的助力，一款新冷冻甜品从测试到面向消费者上市，也可能需要长达两年的时间。

10
00:01:28,610 --> 00:01:32,300
And demand is only going up.
冰淇淋的需求还在持续增长。

11
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:43,620
According to the food packaging company Tetra Pak, more than 25 billion litres of ice cream were eaten worldwide in 2021.
据利乐食品包装公司的数据显示，2021年全球冰淇淋的消费量超过250亿升。

12
00:01:43,620 --> 00:02:01,070
While the US and China are the biggest consumers, data from NielsenIQ shows that people in the UK bought 28% more ice cream during the UK's record-breaking summer compared to a year earlier.
美国和中国是最大的消费市场，而尼尔森IQ的数据表明，在英国创纪录高温的那个夏天，人们购买的冰淇淋数量与去年同时期相比增长了28%。

13
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:10,700
Clearly, rising temperatures can explain why some people are buying more ice cream, but it's not the only explanation.
显然，气温上升是冰淇淋销量增加的原因之一，但这并非唯一的因素。

14
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:19,840
The pandemic has seen people reaching for pleasures they can enjoy at home, which include eating indulgent foods.
疫情期间，人们更倾向于寻求可以在家享受的乐趣，吃些解馋的美食便是其中之一。

15
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:29,990
And worries about the cost-of-living crisis could have a similar effect, as even a premium ice cream is an affordable treat.
而对生活成本危机的担忧也可能产生类似的影响，因为即便是高端冰淇淋，也算得上是一种价格亲民的享受。

16
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:35,350
So, what new things can we expect on a stick or in a cone?
那么，未来我们能在冰淇淋棒或蛋筒里吃到些什么新花样呢？

17
00:02:35,350 --> 00:02:47,180
Consumers of all ages buy ice cream, but it is millennial consumers who are driving interest in more original flavours, including spices.
各个年龄段的消费者都会购买冰淇淋，但正是千禧一代消费者推动了人们对更具创意的口味的兴趣，包括添加香料的冰淇淋。

18
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:58,480
Dairy still dominates, but plant-based ice cream, sorbets and low-calorie choices are a growing part of the frozen dessert market.
乳制品冰淇淋仍占据主导地位，但植物基冰淇淋、果汁冰沙和低热量冰淇淋在冷冻甜品市场的占比正不断提升。

19
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:11,890
But, according to Elsebeth Baungaard, portfolio manager at Tetra Pak, the next global trend will be less about innovation and more about portion size.
不过，利乐公司的投资组合经理埃尔斯贝思·邦高指出，下一个全球趋势将不再侧重于创新，而是聚焦分量。

20
00:03:11,890 --> 00:03:19,580
"I'm sorry to say it's simply shrinking", she says. "But the quality will be higher."
“很遗憾地说，分量确实在变小，”她表示，“但品质会变得更高。”
